📌 What is Wireshark?
Wireshark is a network protocol analyzer used to capture and analyze packets in real-time or from saved files (PCAP).

⚠️ Important Points
❌ Not an IDS (Intrusion Detection System)
❌ Does NOT modify packets
✅ Only captures & analyzes traffic
✅ Requires manual analysis

🎯 Use Cases
🔍 Network troubleshooting
🔐 Security analysis
📚 Protocol learning

📦 PCAP File
PCAP (Packet Capture) is a file format used to store captured network traffic.

🖥️ Wireshark GUI Components
Toolbar → Start/Stop capture
Display Filter Bar → Apply filters
Packet List Pane → Packet summary
Packet Details Pane → Protocol breakdown
Packet Bytes Pane → Hex + ASCII view
Status Bar → Packet count & interface

🎨 Packet Coloring
Helps identify protocols quickly
Two types:
Temporary rules
Permanent rules

📡 Packet Sniffing
▶️ Start → Blue button
⛔ Stop → Red button
🔄 Restart → Green button

🔍 Filters
📌 Display Filters
Used after capture
http
ip.addr == 192.168.1.1
tcp.port == 80

📌 Capture Filters
Used before capture
port 80
host 192.168.1.1

⚔️ Capture vs Display Filter
Feature	Capture Filter	Display Filter
Applied	Before capture	After capture
Purpose	Reduce data	Filter view
Example	port 80	http

🧠 Core Concepts
📦 Packet-Small unit of data transmitted over network
🌐 Protocol-Rules for communication (HTTP, TCP, DNS)
📡 Packet Sniffing-Capturing network traffic
🔌 Network Interface-Connection point (eth0, ens33, lo)

🔐 Security Concepts
❓ Can Wireshark detect attacks?
❌ No (manual analysis required)

❓ Can it decrypt HTTPS?
✅ Yes (if TLS keys available)

❓ Can it modify traffic?
❌ No

🧩 Modes
Promiscuous Mode-Captures all packets in the network

